# CV writing

`cv.md` is the source of truth. When editing it (or proposing a rewrite in CV chat):

- **Professional Summary: 2–3 lines.** Who you are, where you work (backend / distributed systems / observability / data), Python and Go. Stop there.
- **Do not** put Prometheus/Thanos/Grafana stacks, Kafka throughput, SLA details, or LLM metrics in the summary. Those are Experience bullets.
- **Experience is the CV.** Verb-first points, one outcome per bullet, named systems and numbers visible. Senior register, first person or verb-first — not slogans, not essays.
- Do not change an employer job title unless it already appears in `cv.md`.
- Never invent facts. If it is not in `cv.md` or the user said it in this conversation, omit it.
